          'Sinus Augmentation',
          'Sinus Lift Surgery',
          'Maxillary Sinus Floor Augmentation',
        ],
        procedureType: 'https://schema.org/SurgicalProcedure',
        bodyLocation: 'Upper jaw / maxillary sinus',
        preparation:
          'CBCT cone-beam scan to map bone height and sinus anatomy in three dimensions, measuring the exact graft volume needed before treatment begins.',
        howPerformed:
          'Under local anesthesia (sedation available), a small gum incision exposes the bone above the sinus; the sinus membrane is gently lifted, graft material (synthetic, bovine, or autogenous) is packed into the space beneath it, and sutures close the incision. Bone integration takes 4 to 6 months before implants are placed; simultaneous implant placement is possible when adequate existing bone is present.',
        followup:
